;; agentkit — what a program needs to work with a coding agent, whichever model runs it:
;; one event vocabulary every backend reports in, tools as data (served over MCP or offered
;; as function definitions), and the Claude Code backend, which runs the `claude` CLI on the
;; user's SUBSCRIPTION and never on an API key. Shared by bedit-agent and anything else that
;; drives an agent; it knows nothing of either.
(project
  :name "agentkit"
  :version "0.1.1"
  :brood ">= 0.51.0"
  :description
    "Coding-agent plumbing for Brood programs: one event vocabulary for every backend, tools as data (MCP or function definitions), and a Claude Code backend that runs the claude CLI on the user's subscription only."
  :repository "https://github.com/broodlang/agentkit"
  :source-paths ["src"])
